{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "on-design-saved",
  "description": "DLC SuperCharge D-minus: fires when a Kiro Spec design.md is saved. Advances state.md through Phase 2c -> 3 (produce-tech-design, WI-x/D-x/R-x propagation, 4-dim review dispatch). Shell work is consolidated into dlc_bridge.hooks.on_design_saved (Python module) to avoid Kiro shell-execution buffer corruption.",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [".kiro/specs/**/design.md"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "DLC SuperCharge - On Design Saved (Phase 2c -> 3 chain).\n\nStep 0 (notify the user IMMEDIATELY, BEFORE any Bash or other tool call): Surface this exact line as plain chat text so Kiro renders it visibly in the conversation:\n\n  ⏳ DLC: starting produce-tech-design in the background — typically 5–10 minutes. Don't re-prompt; I will surface results when the bridge completes.\n\nThis is essential: Kiro chat does not stream the long-running Bash subprocess output, so without this pre-flight notice the user sees an idle chat and assumes the task is finished.\n\nStep 1 (init): Use Bash to run exactly this single command (no chaining):\n\n  uv run python -m dlc_bridge.hooks.on_design_saved --source <triggering-file>\n\nCapture stdout. The wrapper prints KEY=value lines and ends with one of: PROBE_DEBOUNCED, HOOK_INIT_SKIPPED, BRIDGE_FAILED, or HOOK_INIT_DONE.\n\n- PROBE_DEBOUNCED: another fire is in flight, stop silently.\n- HOOK_INIT_SKIPPED with DESIGN_SKELETON: surface 'Design is still a skeleton - chain skipped. I will re-run when there is more content.' and stop.\n- HOOK_INIT_SKIPPED with PROBE_SELF_FIRE: stop silently — this fire was triggered by our own previous write to design.md (id_propagate) and there is no new work to do. See Issue #8.\n- BRIDGE_FAILED: surface BRIDGE_EXIT and the bridge's stderr to the user, then stop.\n- Otherwise parse SLUG, TECH_DESIGN, and any REVIEW_AVAILABLE entries.\n\nStep 2 (cross-check, no new reviews): Phase 2b reviews already ran once during on-requirements-saved. The SDLC orchestrator's design does NOT re-run reviews on the tech-design; it only verifies the tech-design addresses prior Phase 2b findings. Read any REVIEW_AVAILABLE reports emitted by the wrapper (Phase 2b reports under .dlc/<slug>/analysis_output/). For each Critical / High finding, check whether the enriched tech-design.md addresses it (via a design decision D-x, work item WI-x, or explicit deferral with rationale). Surface unaddressed findings as warnings: 'Tech-design did not reflect <finding>. Review .dlc/<slug>/analysis_output/<file>.'\n\nIf no REVIEW_AVAILABLE entries exist (no Phase 2b reviews were triggered for this scope), skip the cross-check entirely.\n\nStep 3 (finalize: advance state to Phase 3): Use Bash to run:\n\n  uv run python -m dlc_bridge.hooks.on_design_saved --source <triggering-file> --stage finalize\n\nExpect HOOK_FINALIZE_DONE.\n\nStep 4 (surface): Print a 3-line summary: 'Phase 2c->3 chain complete for <slug>. Tech-design: <TECH_DESIGN>. Cross-checked against Phase 2b findings: <addressed-count>/<total>.' End with <HOOK_DONE>."
  }
}
